Description: long-audio player with multi-line waveform and markers
 Audinux is an audio player built for long recordings, from a few minutes
 to multi-hour audiobooks, sermons, lectures and podcasts.
 .
 It renders the whole file as a multi-line waveform that fits the window,
 so any position can be reached with a single click, even in files several
 hours long. Waveforms are generated in the background while playback
 starts immediately and are cached on disk for faster reopening.
 .
 It also provides named markers saved per file, an A-B loop between two
 markers, a playlist, and adjustable playback speed and volume. Playback
 is done by VLC from the original file, without re-encoding.
